{"name":"Tuileries Tint","hex":"#b89cbc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tuileries Palace","blocks":[{"text":"The Tuileries Palace was a palace in Paris which stood on the right bank of the Seine, directly in the west-front of the Louvre Palace. It was the Parisian residence of most French monarchs, from Henri IV to Napoleon III, until it was burned by the Paris Commune in 1871 and demolished in 1883."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Le_Palais_des_Tuileries_-_Le_Gray.jpg/330px-Le_Palais_des_Tuileries_-_Le_Gray.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuileries_Palace"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Vue_des_Tuileries%2C_avant_les_modifications_apport%C3%A9es_par_Levau_-_Gallica_2007_%28adjusted1%29.jpg/1280px-Vue_des_Tuileries%2C_avant_les_modifications_apport%C3%A9es_par_Levau_-_Gallica_2007_%28adjusted1%29.jpg?utm_source=en